  "notes": "Inventory is the complete developer-facing surface added by the feature per the spec PR: one enum and one optional dictionary member. The surrounding base-API surface (Profiler, ProfilerInitOptions, ProfilerTrace, the js-profiling Document Policy) predates this feature (Chrome 94), is documented on MDN, and is covered here as context on the overview (#existing-api), not inventoried. The capture-a-marker / filter-a-marker algorithms are spec machinery with no direct developer-facing entry point; their observable behavior is documented under the marker field's and enum's context/errors/security dimensions and the overview's #exposure-model. The spec PR is unmerged: the published spec contains no marker surface (grep verified 2026-09-13), and every page discloses this. GitHub HTML pages return 403 through this build environment's proxy; PR #89 was verified by fetching refs/pull/89/head via git and confirming it is not an ancestor of main, markers.md and the MSEdge explainer were verified via raw.githubusercontent.com at main, and the demo repo via git ls-remote."
